    "result_text": "The build is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule for owner creation, following the existing count-based conventions in the codebase (mirroring `countOwnersByName`):\n\n1. **`ClinicService.java`** \u2014 added `int countOwnersByCity(String city)` to the service interface.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 implemented `countOwnersByCity` as a read-only transactional method that counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (same idiom as `countOwnersByName`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, added a check that returns `409 CONFLICT` when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, placed alongside the existing conflict checks.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`, which fills a fresh city to 50 owners then expects the 51st to be rejected) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
